commit 19c61eea45ca526f75490ecd45dbea46672a20cf
Author: ledger <ledger@example.invalid>
Date:   Mon Nov 23 01:36:16 2026 +0000

    Add tasks board and polytunnel rota board
    
    The 12 Nov minutes asked for the task sheet as a board "the way the events
    are", so the Thursday meeting is no longer a read-through.
    
    Tasks board: one section per person, so each member can find "what's mine"
    and Hal never has to scroll sideways. Unowned jobs come first as "Nobody
    yet", because unowned jobs are what keeps going wrong (the gutter, the
    water meter). Done jobs go into a fold at the bottom (Tomas's request).
    Grouped by person, not by due week: the page is static, so "due this
    week" headings would be wrong by the next meeting, but names don't change.
    
    Polytunnel rota: its own board, because the sheet mixed it into two
    unrelated side columns and Dot wants to check it at the gate. This week
    is at the top, earlier weeks fold away. Each week is keyed by its Sunday
    so the current week stays visible until the week is over.
    
    Two fixes to the export's data: "Done" -> "done" (tool shed inventory;
    otherwise it counted as open) and "priya" -> "Priya" (seed potatoes;
    otherwise she got a second section).
    
    kit/board.py: new optional settings only (optional section date, label
    for a blank section, done fold, next-badge label, date/prefix columns, no
    "to do" count without a status column). The events board rebuilds
    byte-for-byte the same.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

